                <pb facs="0609" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1751: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-07T00:00:00-03:00">March 7,
                        1940—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received March 8—1:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. Resumption of services on the Brazilian foreign debt on the plan specified in
                    the Department’s telegrams 51, March 4, 9 p.m. and 56, March 6, 7 p.m. is
                    provided for in a decree-law in the following text which the Minister of Finance
                    says will be signed by the President tonight. This is to be held confidential
                    until released for publication here probably tomorrow.</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of Decree-Law 2,085 approved March 8, 1940. See Brazil,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Diario Oficial</hi>, March 9, 1940, page 4150.]</p>
                <p>Before receiving the Department’s 57, March 7, 1 p.m., I had already persuaded
                    Aranha to drop the idea of raising Grade IV above the foregoing figures.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
